# OrCAD Capture / PSpice automation

## Before touching Capture
- Confirm the active design first; it changes between jobs (`orcadcpmtest\1\`, `joeldesign`, ...). Run `python scripts/query_capture.py` (page, design, part count). Projects live under `%APPDATA%\SPB_Data\cdssetup\workspace\projects\`.
- Resuming a lab or homework circuit? Read `labs/STATUS.md` for what is already on the page.
- Look up every part in `parts_catalog.json` (`describe_part('VSIN')`) and reuse `placement_lib` recipes and pin offsets from `pin_offsets.json`. Don't rediscover OLB paths.
- If port 9020 stops answering, run `python scripts/restart_capture.py` (relaunches Capture and waits for the port).
- Send any Tcl containing `$` through the Python helpers (`dump_page.tcl`), not PowerShell, which eats `$vars`.

## Crash-safe sending
- One Tcl command per send, trailing `\n`; batches: PlacePart ≤2 (BJT 1), PlaceWire ≤3, Delete ≤4, with catalog delays (~100–180 ms).
- Order: one PlacePart → `Menu {File::Save}` → next part; then grounds; then wires (`send_all` in `hw_bessel_lpf.py` / `lab2_place.py` is the reference).
- Delete one `DeletePartInst` / `DeleteWire` / `DeleteGlobal` at a time with a pause, and do **not** save mid delete-loop.
- Keep origins inside `page.safe_xy_inches` (~0.4–10.5 × 0.4–7.5"); off-page parts are invisible.

## Never via Tcl (crash or hang)
- Bulk delete, `Edit::Select All` + Delete, `DeleteGlobal` loops, `BringToFront`
- `SetRotation` (hangs); place R/C horizontal and route wires instead
- `SetLocation` on grounds/globals
- `PlacePart` of `marker.etc` / advanced markers; add markers manually
- `VPULSE` placement; place `VDC` and patch the pulse spec into the `.cir`
- Fairchild `2N7000` prop edits; use `MbreakN` + MODEL `2N7000`
- `tex_inst.olb` bare `TL074` (ORCAP-1687 modal blocks port 9020); use `"TL074/301/TI" "A"`, dismiss modal via `lab2_try_tl074.py`
- Giant `source` scripts, CorSimSrvr / `orTclNewSimProfile`

## Wiring
- Wire pin tip to pin tip using cached offsets. A wire that passes **through** another pin hotspot connects to it.
- Never run vertically along an op-amp OUT column or through the other terminal of a source; give parallel caps separate drops.
- Grounds: `PlaceGround` capsym `"0"` `"0"`, hotspot X aligned, wire straight down from above.
- `PlaceNetAlias` must land exactly on a wire segment.
- VDC: set both `DC` and `VALUE` (`15Vdc`), or the netlist emits `0Vdc`.

## Simulation
- Create profiles in the Capture UI (PSpice → New Simulation Profile), then patch the `.sim` on disk (`sim_lib`). Hand-edited `.opj` GUIDs are silently dropped.
- Netlist: `Menu {PSpice::Create Netlist}`. Headless: `C:\Cadence\OrCADX_25.1\tools\bin\psp_cmd.exe` with absolute `.lib` paths; kill it after `JOB CONCLUDED`.
- In `.PRINT`/`.PROBE` use `V([VOUT])` or numeric nodes; bare `V(VOUT)` is read as a device.
- Post-process with the MATLAB MCP (`load_pspice_csv`) or `sim_lib` plots. For quick standalone checks of a topology, the LTspice MCP is faster than building in Capture.

## After finishing a circuit
Update `labs/STATUS.md` (what's on which page, profile names, results paths) and add any new crash trigger to this rule and `parts_catalog.json` → `crash_rules`.
